{title: 613 - Fight the Good Fight}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #613 • PENTECOST • L.M.}
{lyricist: John S. B. Monsell}
{composer: William Boyd}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 613}
{meta: tune PENTECOST}
{meta: meter L.M.}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Fight the good fight with [D]all [G/D]thy [D7]might;
[G]Christ [Bm]is thy strength, [D7/C]and [Am]Christ thy [F#dim]right;
[Bm]Lay hold [Am]on [G]life [G#m]and [Am]it shall be
[F#dim]Thy joy and [G]crown [C]eternally.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Run the straight race through [D]God's [G/D]good [D7]grace;
[G]Lift [Bm]up thine eyes, [D7/C]and [Am]seek His [F#dim]face.
[Bm]Life with [Am]its [G]path [G#m]before [Am]us lies;
[F#dim]Christ is the [G]way, [C]and Christ [D/A]the [G]prize.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Cast care aside, lean [D]on [G/D]thy [D7]guide,
[G]His [Bm]boundless mercy [Am]will provide;
[Bm]Trust, and [Am]the [G]trusting [Am]soul shall prove
[F#dim]Christ is its [G]life, [C]and Christ [D/A]its [G]love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Faint not, nor fear, His [D]arms [G/D]are [D7]near;
[G]He [Bm]changeth not, [D7/C]and [Am]thou art [F#dim]dear.
[Bm]Only [Am]believe, [G#m]and [Am]thou shalt see
[F#dim]That Christ is [G]all [C]in all [D/A]to [G]thee.
{end_of_verse}
